# A row delete that fails after its group expired is tried again (odi-oss
# #248). The group leaves the table when it expires, so walking the table
# again would never reach it: the failed delete is kept aside and retried with
# the next resync, five seconds on while it keeps failing, and the state shows
# nothing stale once it went through. Membership is 65 s (2 x 30 + 5): the
# join at 10 expires at 75.
0 policy
snooping=1
igmp_function=0
immediate_leave=0
robustness=2
query_interval=30
query_max_response=5
end
0 tick
10 v2join 1 0 192.168.1.10 239.1.1.1
74 hwfail 2
75 tick
79 tick
80 tick
81 state
# The same, but the group comes back before the retry: the retry writes the
# row with its members instead of deleting it (and the walk of the table writes
# it once more, the same row). The join at 100 expires at 165.
100 v2join 1 0 192.168.1.10 239.2.2.2
164 hwfail 2
165 tick
167 v2join 1 0 192.168.1.10 239.2.2.2
170 tick
171 state
